<p>NOTES: Operating earnings for second quarter were $280.4 million or $0.70 per share compared with $213.0 million or $0.56 per share in 1996 quarter.</p>
<p>Net income/loss includes $4.4 million and $38.2 million in realized investment losses for the 1997 and 1996 quarters, respectively, and $391.0 million of net charges related to the acquisition and integration of Aetna property casualty businesses in the second quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>Per share results are bvased on 398.5 million and 374.5 mnillion average shares outstanding during the 1997 and 1996 quarters, respectively.</p>
<p>Financial data for Travelers Casualty and Surety Co, formerly Aetna Casualty and Surety Co and Standard Fire Insurance Co, is included from date of acquisition (April 2, 1996).</p>
<p>--((New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
